-- The quantities the definitions in Annexes 1 to 3 state a threshold for. A witness of
-- ordinary competence (the treating specialist, a laboratory report) states each one.
DECLARE `A measured quantity` IS ONE OF
    `hours without response to external stimuli`
    `days after the coma at which the permanent neurological deficit is assessed`
    `MMSE score out of 30`
    `months the qualifying state has lasted`
    `weeks the qualifying state has lasted`
    `days the qualifying state has lasted`
    `eGFR in ml per minute per 1.73 square metres of body surface`
    `number of activities of daily living the insured cannot perform`
    `number of named coronary arteries narrowed by at least 60%`
    `number of named coronary arteries narrowed by at least 75%`
    `NYHA class`
    `aortic diameter in mm`
    `percentage of body surface with second-degree burns`
    `percentage of the face with third-degree burns`
    `percentage of body surface with third-degree burns`
    `percentage of body surface with skin grafts after burns`
    `hearing loss in decibels at all frequencies`
    `visual acuity as a Snellen fraction`
    `visual field in degrees`
    `hours of continuous mechanical ventilation`
    `percentage narrowing of the carotid artery`
    `HAI-Knodell fibrosis score`
    `Child-Pugh score`
    `creatinine clearance per minute`
    `number of the listed clinical signs present`
    `number of the listed laboratory tests positive`
    `grand mal seizures per week`
    `number of anti-epileptic drugs prescribed`
    `weeks of inpatient treatment`
    `FEV1 in litres`
    `resting PaO2 in mmHg`
    `episodes of pancreatitis`
    `bowel segments resected`
    `major joints affected`
    `bone density T-score`
    `osteoporotic fractures of the femur, wrist or spine`
    `limbs whose use is entirely lost`
    `months within which the illness is expected to cause death`
    `clotting factor VIII or IX as a percentage`
    `coronary artery dilation or aneurysm in mm`
    `proteinuria in grams per day`
    `completed weeks of pregnancy at the fetal death`
    `days from the birth to the death of the child`
    `metres of small bowel transplanted`
    `thyroid tumour diameter in cm`
    `Breslow thickness in mm`
    `Clark level`
    `RAI stage`
    `whole liver lobes removed`
    `number of the four heart attack criteria met`
    `myasthenia gravis clinical class`
    `WHO lupus nephritis class`
    `days from the incident to notice to the Company`
    `days from the incident to seroconversion`
    `days from the incident to the negative HIV antibody test`

-- The causes the definitions in Annex 1 exclude, each named in at least one "Loại trừ"
-- sentence (the cause table in cstd-annex-tables.l4 quotes each sentence).
DECLARE `A cause` IS ONE OF
    `alcohol`
    `medicines or drugs`
    `addictive substances`
    `toxins`
    `HIV infection`
    `a self-inflicted injury`
    `a psychological or psychiatric cause without organic damage`
    `diabetes`
    `poliomyelitis`
    `systemic lupus erythematosus`
    `an accident or injury`
    `gallstones or cholecystitis`
    `kidney donation`
    `growth hormone treatment`
-- END GENERATED

-- A reading the specialist or the laboratory reports, of one quantity.
DECLARE `A measurement` HAS
    `the quantity` IS A `A measured quantity`
    `the value`    IS A NUMBER

-- The six activities of daily living the late-stage annex defines, which several middle- and
-- late-stage definitions count ("2 trong 6", "3 trong 6").
